cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the data sources it relies on (LOLA, NAIF DE440, Hayne et al. 2017)."
title: "ArtemisThermalBase: illumination and regolith temperature for lunar polar terrain"
version: 0.5.0
date-released: 2026-10-13
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/SpaceEngineerSS/ArtemisThermalBase"
url: "https://spaceengineerss.github.io/ArtemisThermalBase/"
abstract: >-
  ArtemisThermalBase computes illumination and subsurface temperature over
  lunar polar terrain. It traces shadows to an extended solar disk through a
  bounding-volume hierarchy on LOLA topography lowered onto the lunar sphere,
  takes the Sun from NAIF SPICE, and advances a one-dimensional regolith
  column with temperature- and depth-dependent properties under every facet.
  Outputs include temperature extremes, sunlit time and water-ice stability.
keywords:
  - Moon
  - lunar south pole
  - illumination
  - thermal model
  - ray tracing
  - cold traps
  - water ice
authors:
  - family-names: "Gümüş"
    given-names: "Mehmet"
